     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Welcome & Introduction"
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer",
     "height": 10
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Call to Worship"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We worship with Christians near and far,",
      [
       "Christ’s reign gathers us into one body.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God’s word is for all of us.",
      [
       "May it be a lamp to our feet",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and a light to our path.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Christ, our true and gentle King,",
      "speak to us",
      "that we may hear your upside-down kingdom.",
      [
       "Move among us",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "that we may behold your liberating glory.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Receive our prayers",
      [
       "that we may learn to trust your way of justice and peace.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving God’s Mercy",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Invitation to Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In the presence of Christ our servant-King,",
      "we recognise the places where our lives fall short of love."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Trusting his mercy, justice, and gentleness,",
      "let us bring our whole selves to God in confession."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Loving God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we admit that we have done wrong:",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in our thoughts, words, and actions.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Please forgive us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Help us to change,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and guide us in the future.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Help us to live justly,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to show mercy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and to walk humbly with you.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Absolution"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God, the Source of mercy and renewal,",
      "forgives you and sets you free."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Christ restores you in his likeness,",
      "that your life may reflect love and goodness."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Holy Spirit strengthens you to walk the way of justice and peace."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Giving Praise",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Giving Praise"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give thanks to you, gracious God,",
      [
       "for your mercy restores and your grace makes us whole.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You have drawn near in every age—",
      [
       "freeing the captives, forgiving the broken, feeding the hungry.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "From the beginning you made the world in goodness,",
      [
       "a gift of grace where salvation is written in every living thing.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Jesus, your Word became flesh,",
      [
       "bringing salvation to the world and grace upon grace.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "By your Spirit, you breathe life into our weary souls",
      [
       "and set us again on the path of joy.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give you thanks and praise,",
      [
       "now and always. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Prayer of the Day",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayer of the Day"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Shepherd King,",
      "you seek the lost and bind up the wounded,",
      "and wait for us in the hungry, the stranger and the prisoner.",
      "Open our eyes to see you where you have promised to be,",
      "and our hands to serve you there,",
      "until your reign of justice and peace is complete;",
      "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Ezekiel 34",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Readings"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Readings are from the Common English Bible.",
     "margin": "16px 0 0"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Ezekiel 34:11–16, 20–24",
     "sub": "First reading",
     "margin": "30px 0 18px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "A reading from the prophet Ezekiel."
     ],
     "margin": "0 0 20px"
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "margin": "0 0 22px",
     "paragraphs": [
      "The Lord God proclaims: I myself will search for my flock and seek them out. As a shepherd seeks out the flock when some in the flock have been scattered, so will I seek out my flock. I will rescue them from all the places where they were scattered during the time of clouds and thick darkness. I will gather and lead them out from the countries and peoples, and I will bring them to their own fertile land. I will feed them on Israel’s highlands, along the riverbeds, and in all the inhabited places. I will feed them in good pasture, and their sheepfold will be there, on Israel’s lofty highlands. On Israel’s highlands, they will lie down in a secure fold and feed on green pastures. I myself will feed my flock and make them lie down. This is what the Lord God says. I will seek out the lost, bring back the strays, bind up the wounded, and strengthen the weak. But the fat and the strong I will destroy, because I will tend my sheep with justice.",
      "So the Lord God proclaims to them: I will judge between the fat and the lean sheep. You shove with shoulder and flank, and with your horns you ram all the weak sheep until you’ve scattered them outside. But I will rescue my flock so that they will never again be prey. I will even judge between the sheep! I will appoint for them a single shepherd, and he will feed them. My servant David will feed them. He will be their shepherd. I, the Lord, will be their God, and my servant David will be their prince. I, the Lord, have spoken."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "This is the word of the Lord",
      [
       "Thanks be to God",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Gospel",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Gospel"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Matthew 25:31–46",
     "margin": "22px 0 18px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "Alleluia! ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "When you have done it for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of mine, you have done it for me, says the Lord. ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "A reading from the Good News according to Matthew.",
      [
       "Glory to you Lord Jesus Christ",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "margin": "0 0 22px",
     "paragraphs": [
      "“Now when the Human One comes in his majesty and all his angels are with him, he will sit on his majestic throne. All the nations will be gathered in front of him. He will separate them from each other, just as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats. He will put the sheep on his right side. But the goats he will put on his left.",
      "“Then the king will say to those on his right, ‘Come, you who will receive good things from my Father. Inherit the kingdom that was prepared for you before the world began. I was hungry and you gave me food to eat. I was thirsty and you gave me a drink. I was a stranger and you welcomed me. I was naked and you gave me clothes to wear. I was sick and you took care of me. I was in prison and you visited me.’",
      "“Then those who are righteous will reply to him, ‘Lord, when did we see you hungry and feed you, or thirsty and give you a drink? When did we see you as a stranger and welcome you, or naked and give you clothes to wear? When did we see you sick or in prison and visit you?’",
      "“Then the king will reply to them, ‘I assure you that when you have done it for one of the least of these brothers and sisters of mine, you have done it for me.’",
      "“Then he will say to those on his left, ‘Get away from me, you who will receive terrible things. Go into the unending fire that has been prepared for the devil and his angels. I was hungry and you didn’t give me food to eat. I was thirsty and you didn’t give me anything to drink. I was a stranger and you didn’t welcome me. I was naked and you didn’t give me clothes to wear. I was sick and in prison, and you didn’t visit me.’",
      "“Then they will reply, ‘Lord, when did we see you hungry or thirsty or a stranger or naked or sick or in prison and didn’t do anything to help you?’ Then he will answer, ‘I assure you that when you haven’t done it for one of the least of these, you haven’t done it for me.’ And they will go away into eternal punishment. But the righteous ones will go into eternal life.”"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "This is the good news of the Lord",
      [
       "Praise to you Lord Jesus Christ",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sermon & Affirmation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Ministry of the Word"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Sermon"
    },
    {
     "type": "spacer",
     "height": 10
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Affirmation"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in God the Father,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose love gives room for creation,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose mercy restores all,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and whose promise holds creation fast.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through whom all creation is made—",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "the Word made flesh,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "friend of the outcast,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "light in the darkness,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "risen and true.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in the Spirit who moves among us,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "who brings life to dust,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "stirs courage,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "kindles compassion,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and weaves us into one.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe the Church is a living body,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "open to all,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "rooted in grace,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and sent to serve in love.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "This is our faith,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our calling,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our love.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
