  {
   "label": "Offertory Hymn",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Offertory Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Christ Be Our Light"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "SoG 787 · verses 1, 3, 4 & 5 with chorus",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Longing for light, we wait in darkness",
       "Longing for truth, we turn to You.",
       "Make us Your own, Your holy people",
       "Light for the world to see."
      ],
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Longing for food, many are hungry",
       "Longing for water, many still thirst.",
       "Make us Your bread, broken for others",
       "Shared until all are fed."
      ],
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Longing for shelter, many are homeless",
       "Longing for warmth, many are cold.",
       "Make us Your building, sheltering others",
       "Walls made of living stone."
      ],
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Many the gift, many the people",
       "Many the hearts that yearn to belong.",
       "Let us be servants to one another",
       "Making Your kingdom come."
      ],
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Introduction to Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Introduction to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come to this table,",
      "where Christ our servant-King",
      "gathers all people into a kingdom",
      "shaped by mercy and justice."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Here we taste the freedom of his reign",
      "and share in the life that makes us whole."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you.",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Lift up your hearts.",
      [
       "We lift them to the Lord.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.",
      [
       "It is right to give our thanks and praise.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Preface",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Preface"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "It is right to give you thanks,",
      "God of justice and mercy."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You created the world in love,",
      "giving us land, water, people, and purpose.",
      "You called us into freedom and community,",
      [
       "to reflect the life of your kingdom.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "When we turned from your way, you did not abandon us.",
      "Through prophets you confronted injustice.",
      [
       "You opened paths toward healing and hope.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Jesus, our servant-King,",
      "you walked among us—teaching, restoring,",
      "and revealing a reign where the lowly are lifted.",
      [
       "In you we discover glory.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "So with all who long for freedom",
      "and with all who hope for your kingdom’s renewal,",
      "we give you thanks and praise, saying together:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Blessed is Christ our King,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose power is mercy",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and whose reign lifts the forgotten.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Blessed is our God, forever.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Words of Institution",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Words of Institution"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "On the night of his giving,",
      "Jesus blessed and broke the bread.",
      "He shared it with his friends, saying:",
      "Take and eat.",
      "This is my body, broken for you.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Wine"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "After they had eaten,",
      "he took the cup of wine,",
      "gave thanks, and said:",
      "Drink this, all of you.",
      "This is my blood of the new covenant,",
      "poured out for you and for all,",
      "to reconcile and to heal.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Acclamation to Sanctus",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Acclamation"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Let us proclaim the mystery of faith."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Christ has died to set us free.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ is risen to make us whole.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ will come again with justice and joy.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Epiclesis"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come, Holy Spirit,",
      "rest upon these gifts of bread and wine,",
      "that they may be for us the life of Christ."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "As we share this meal,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "make us one with each other,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and one in Christ, our risen Lord",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Doxology"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Gathered with angels and archangels,",
      "and with every generation who has trusted your love,",
      "we join the hymn of heaven:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Holy, holy, holy Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "God of power and might,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Heaven and earth are full of your glory.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Praise to you in the highest.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Lord’s Prayer to Invitation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "The Lord’s Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Father, uphold the holiness of your name.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Bring in your kingdom.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Give us the bread we need for today.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Forgive us our sins,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we also forgive everyone who has wronged us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "And save us in times of trial.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "For you are worthy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our Lord and God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to receive glory and honour and power,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "because you created all things.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Breaking the Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We break and share this bread,",
      "a sign of Christ’s life poured out for us."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Though we are many, we are made one,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we all eat of the one bread.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Invitation to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The gifts of God for the people of God."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Graciously nourish us, O Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "so that we who try to follow you",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "may receive food for the journey",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and be bound in solidarity",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "with all who walk in your way",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Communion Anthem",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Communion Anthem"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Jesus Christ, Be the Wine of Grace"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Sung by all",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "In the singing, in the silence,",
       "in the hands expectant, open,",
       "in the blessing, in the breaking,",
       "in the presence at this table"
      ],
      [
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ],
      [
       "In the question, in the answer,",
       "in the moment of acceptance,",
       "in the heart’s cry, in the healing,",
       "in the circle of your people."
      ],
      [
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Rejoice, the Lord is King"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 216 · verses 1–5",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Rejoice, the Lord is King;",
       "your Lord and King adore;",
       "let all give thanks, and sing,",
       "and triumph evermore:",
       "Lift up your heart,",
       "lift up your voice,",
       "Rejoice, again I say, rejoice!"
      ],
      [
       "Jesus the Saviour, reigns,",
       "the God of truth and love;",
       "when he had purged our stains,",
       "he took his seat above:",
       "Lift up your heart,",
       "lift up your voice,",
       "Rejoice, again I say, rejoice!"
      ],
      [
       "His kingdom cannot fail,",
       "he rules o'er earth and heaven;",
       "the keys of death and hell",
       "are to our Jesus given:",
       "Lift up your heart,",
       "lift up your voice,",
       "Rejoice, again I say, rejoice!"
      ],
      [
       "He sits at God’s right hand",
       "till all his foes submit,",
       "and bow to his command,",
       "and fall beneath his feet:",
       "Lift up your heart,",
       "lift up your voice,",
       "Rejoice, again I say, rejoice!"
      ],
      [
       "Rejoice in glorious hope!",
       "Jesus, the Judge, shall come,",
       "and take his servants up",
       "to their eternal home.",
       "We soon shall hear",
       "the archangel's voice;",
       "the trump of God shall sound, Rejoice!"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Out",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayer after Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God our liberator and King,",
      "we thank you for feeding us at your table of mercy.",
      "Strengthen us through this holy meal",
      "to walk in the way of Christ’s justice and peace."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Gratitude for Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we have broken your bread",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and received your life.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "By the power of your Spirit",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "keep us always in your love",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Notices"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Parish notices, read by the leader or a warden.",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Blessing & Dismissal",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Blessing"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "May Christ our servant-King guide your steps",
      "with courage, mercy, and justice."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "May his reign of peace take root in your life,",
      "and his compassion shine through all you do."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "And the blessing of God,",
      "Father, Son and Holy Spirit,",
      "be with you always.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Dismissal"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Go in peace, to love and serve the Lord",
      [
       "In the name of Christ. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Hymn",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "You Servants of God"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 215 · verses 1–4",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "You servants of God,",
       "Your Master proclaim,",
       "And publish abroad",
       "His wonderful name;",
       "The name all-victorious",
       "Of Jesus extol;",
       "His kingdom is glorious",
       "And rules over all."
      ],
      [
       "Our God rules on high,",
       "Almighty to save;",
       "And still he is nigh,",
       "His presence we have;",
       "The great congregation",
       "His triumph shall sing,",
       "Ascribing salvation",
       "To Jesus our King."
      ],
      [
       "Salvation to God,",
       "Who sits on the throne!",
       "Let all cry aloud,",
       "And honour the Son;",
       "The praises of Jesus",
       "The angels proclaim,",
       "Fall down on their faces,",
       "And worship the Lamb."
      ],
      [
       "Then let us adore,",
       "And give him his right,",
       "All glory and power,",
       "All wisdom and might,",
       "All honour and blessing,",
       "With angels above,",
       "And thanks never ceasing,",
       "And infinite love."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}